post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'

==> Synaptics 06cb:009a fingerprint reader (libfprint-2-tod1-synaptics009a)

The driver plugin is installed, but the reader needs a ONE-TIME setup before it
will work: the sensor's QMatcher firmware extension has to be flashed, and a
per-sensor host calibration generated.  Both are done by:

    sudo synaptics009a-setup

Then enrol and verify a finger:

    fprintd-enroll -f right-index-finger    # 12 presses; press the oval, lift, vary the angle
    fprintd-verify                          # must print: verify-match

Optionally use the reader for sudo and login too (one reversible line in
/etc/pam.d/system-auth; undo with --undo):

    sudo synaptics009a-pam

Full notes: /usr/share/doc/libfprint-2-tod1-synaptics009a/README.md

EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  post_install
}

pre_remove() {
  cat <<'EOF'

==> The sensor's firmware extension and host calibration are left in place.
    If this reader is no longer wanted, remove the PAM line with:
        sudo synaptics009a-pam --undo

EOF
}
